{"reply":"You can acknowledge the effort without treating it as a reason to give up your voice. For example:

> “I know you’ve been carrying a lot, and I appreciate the work you’ve put into moving this forward. When the plan changed after our planning meetings ended, I felt out of the loop. I’d like to understand what led to the change and have a chance to share my perspective before we settle on the next step. I’m not questioning your commitment—I’m asking to be included in the decision.”

This keeps the focus on the process and your request rather than judging their character. You also don’t have to accept “I’m carrying the burden for us” as proof that your questions are unfair. What part of the plan change most needs your voice right now?","memory":{"kind":"no_memory_candidate","reason_code":"automatic_capture_disabled"}}

